 "readme:fudan-generative-vision/D3D": {
  "fetched_at": "2026-11-05T04:24:29.436Z",
  "bytes": 11424,
  "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"README.md\">English</a> | <a href=\"README.zh-CN.md\">简体中文</a>\n</p>\n\n<h1 align=\"center\">D3D</h1>\n\n<h3 align=\"center\">Decoupled Diffusion Drafting for Asynchronous Speculative Decoding</h3>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <strong>Diffusion drafts. The target verifies. D3D overlaps both.</strong><br>\n  A decoupled draft-and-verify architecture, powered by Qwen3-derived diffusion drafts.\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/collections/fudan-generative-ai/d3d-6ae71f370a3f3b48ff8e4d15\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/Models-D3D_Collection-fbbf24?style=flat-square\" alt=\"D3D model collection\"></a>\n  <a href=\"#quick-start\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/Quick_Start-Get_started-22c55e?style=flat-square\" alt=\"Quick start\"></a>\n  <a href=\"docs/architecture.md\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/Architecture-Docs-0ea5e9?style=flat-square\" alt=\"Architecture guide\"></a>\n  <a href=\"#benchmarking\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/Benchmarks-Protocol-f97316?style=flat-square\" alt=\"Benchmark protocol\"></a>\n</p>\n\n<a id=\"overview\"></a>\n\n## ✨ Overview\n\n**D3D** decouples a diffusion **draft model** from the **target verifier** on\nseparate GPUs. Draft generation overlaps target verification, with verification\nfeedback selecting reusable candidates for the next decoding step.\n\n**The contribution is the D3D execution architecture:** independent drafting,\noverlapped verification, and feedback-driven candidate reuse.\n\n| Asynchronous execution | Parallel diffusion drafts |\n|:---|:---|\n| Drafting and verification run on separate GPUs. | Block-wise candidate generation with packed outcomes. |\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"docs/figure1.png\" alt=\"D3D method overview: drafter training, progressive layer pruning, and asynchronous inference\" width=\"960\">\n</p>\n\n**How it works:** a target-selected anchor starts a parallel diffusion draft;\nthe target verifies the pending block while the draft GPU prepares possible\ncontinuations; verification feedback selects the continuation to reuse.\nSee the [architecture guide](docs/architecture.md) for the execution flow.\n\n<a id=\"model-zoo\"></a>\n\n## 🤗 Model Zoo\n\n**[Browse the D3D collection →](https://huggingface.co/collections/fudan-generative-ai/d3d-6ae71f370a3f3b48ff8e4d15)**\n\nSix Qwen3-derived draft checkpoints are grouped in **fudan-generative-ai / D3D**. These are\n**draft models**, not replacements for the target models. `p` denotes pruning;\n`24D` and `31D` denote the retained transformer-layer counts.\n\n| Target verifier | Draft family | Layers | D3D checkpoint |\n|:---|:---|:---:|:---|\n| [Qwen3-8B](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-8B) | 1.7B | 28 | [D3D-1.7B-8B](https://huggingface.co/fudan-generative-ai/D3D-1.7B-8B) |\n| [Qwen3-8B](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-8B) | 8B | 36 | [D3D-8B-8B](https://huggingface.co/fudan-generative-ai/D3D-8B-8B) |\n| [Qwen3-8B](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-8B) | Pruned 8B | 31 | [D3D-31D-p8B-8B](https://huggingface.co/fudan-generative-ai/D3D-31D-p8B-8B) |\n| [Qwen3-32B](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-32B) | 1.7B | 28 | [D3D-1.7B-32B](https://huggingface.co/fudan-generative-ai/D3D-1.7B-32B) |\n| [Qwen3-32B](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-32B) | 8B | 36 | [D3D-8B-32B](https://huggingface.co/fudan-generative-ai/D3D-8B-32B) |\n| [Qwen3-32B](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-32B) | Pruned 1.7B | 24 | [D3D-24D-p1.7B-32B](https://huggingface.co/fudan-generative-ai/D3D-24D-p1.7B-32B) |\n\n> Checkpoints retain their original FP32 tensors; inference uses BF16.\n> Each Hub repository includes tokenizer assets, inference compatibility code,\n> a model card, and release metadata. The family size in a name is not an exact\n> post-pruning parameter count. Exact source steps, tensor counts, and release\n> compatibility notes are in [checkpoint details](docs/models.md).\n\n<a id=\"installation\"></a>\n\n## 📦 Installation\n\nTraining, layer pruning, and native single-request/concurrent inference share\n**PyTorch 2.8.0**, **Transformers 4.57.3**, **FlashAttention 2.8.3**, and\n**CUDA 12.8**. Python 3.10+ is supported; unified-environment GPU validation used\nPython 3.12 and two NVIDIA H800 80 GB GPUs.\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/linguancong524/D3D.git\ncd D3D\npython -m venv .venv\nsource .venv/bin/activate\npip install -r requirements.txt\npip install flash-attn==2.8.3 --no-build-isolation\npip install -e . --no-deps\n```\n\nInstall PyTorch before building FlashAttention. A matching prebuilt wheel can\nbe used instead; source builds need a CUDA toolkit, a C++ compiler, and\nsufficient host memory. The concurrent backend requires FlashAttention.\nThe optional SGLang backend still requires its separately locked environment;\ndo not install its runtime lock into this environment.\n\n<a id=\"quick-start\"></a>\n\n## 🚀 Quick Start\n\n### 1. Select a target / draft pair\n\n```bash\nexport CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1\n\n# optional: override the defaults for every script\nexport TARGET_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3-8B\nexport DRAFT_MODEL=fudan-generative-ai/D3D-1.7B-8B\n```\n\nThe target runs on `cuda:0`, and the draft runs on `cuda:1`. Model IDs also\naccept local checkpoint directories. Public model downloads do not require\na Hugging Face token.\n\n### 2. Run asynchronous decoding\n\nEvery script forwards extra flags to its Python entry point, so prefer command\nline options over environment variables. Single-request scripts take\n`--verifier` / `--drafter`; concurrent scripts take `--target` / `--draft`.\n\n**Single request** — one MATH-500 sample, up to 128 generated tokens:\n\n```bash\nbash scripts/quickstart_single.sh\n\n# e.g. another pair with a longer generation cap\nbash scripts/quickstart_single.sh \\\n    --verifier Qwen/Qwen3-32B \\\n    --drafter fudan-generative-ai/D3D-24D-p1.7B-32B \\\n    --max-new-tokens 512\n```\n\n**Concurrent requests** — four samples at concurrency 4:\n\n```bash\nbash scripts/quickstart_concurrent.sh\n\n# e.g. concurrency 8 with 256 KV pages\nCONCURRENCY=8 bash scripts/quickstart_concurrent.sh --pages 256\n```\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Use the 32B target with the 24-layer pruned draft</strong></summary>\n\n```bash\nbash scripts/quickstart_single.sh \\\n    --verifier Qwen/Qwen3-32B \\\n    --drafter fudan-generative-ai/D3D-24D-p1.7B-32B\n\nbash scripts/quickstart_concurrent.sh \\\n    --target Qwen/Qwen3-32B \\\n    --draft fudan-generative-ai/D3D-24D-p1.7B-32B \\\n    --concurrency 4 --pages 128\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Useful configuration options</strong></summary>\n\nScripts pass their defaults as flags, and anything appended on the command line\nwins. Only a few environment variables remain:\n\n| Variable | Purpose | Default |\n|:---|:---|:---|\n| `TARGET_MODEL` | Target verifier used by every script | `Qwen/Qwen3-8B` |\n| `DRAFT_MODEL` | Draft checkpoint used by every script | `fudan-generative-ai/D3D-1.7B-8B` |\n| `DATASETS` | Dataset list for the two benchmark scripts | the seven benchmarks |\n| `CONCURRENCY` | Quick-start request count, or benchmark sweep list | `4` / `1 4 8 16` |\n| `D3D_DATA_CACHE` | Optional existing JSONL dataset cache | `data_cache/` |\n\nEverything else is a flag, for example `--max-samples`, `--max-new-tokens`,\n`--block-size`, `--anchor-num`, `--pages` or `--no-baseline`.\n\nUse `python single/eval_async_packed.py --help` or\n`python -m serving.bench --help` for the full set of options.\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"benchmarking\"></a>\n\n## 📊 Benchmarking\n\nRun single-request evaluation over the standard datasets:\n\n```bash\nbash scripts/benchmark.sh\n```\n\nRun concurrent evaluation at request concurrency 1, 4, 8, and 16:\n\n```bash\nbash scripts/benchmark_concurrent.sh\n```\n\nDatasets are downloaded at runtime, not bundled in this repository.\nLiveCodeBench v6 uses `test6.jsonl` from\n`livecodebench/code_generation_lite`; the other datasets use `datasets`.\nSee the [benchmark protocol](benchmarks/README.md) for sources, splits,\ntoken caps, timing boundaries, and reporting rules.\n\n## ⚙️ Inference Engine Support\n\nThe repository supports native D3D inference and an optional two-GPU\nSGLang Hybrid backend. Install SGLang separately:\n\n```bash\nbash scripts/sglang/install.sh\n```\n\nStart the two-GPU backend (GPU 0: Target + local Draft; GPU 1: optional Draft):\n\n```bash\nexport TARGET_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3-8B\nexport DRAFT_MODEL=fudan-generative-ai/D3D-1.7B-8B\nexport TARGET_GPU=0 DRAFT_GPU=1\nexport MAX_RUNNING_REQUESTS=1\nbash scripts/sglang/launch.sh hybrid\n```\n\nThen run a MATH-500 evaluation from another terminal:\n\n```bash\nexport MAX_RUNNING_REQUESTS=1\nexport TARGET_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3-8B\n.venv-sglang/bin/python scripts/sglang/benchmark.py \\\n  --dataset math500 \\\n  --tokenizer \"$TARGET_MODEL\" \\\n  --samples 128 --concurrency \"$MAX_RUNNING_REQUESTS\" \\\n  --repetitions 1 --max-new-tokens 512 \\\n  --output outputs/sglang/example.json\n```\n\nThe dataset is downloaded automatically and cached by Hugging Face Datasets.\n\nSet `MAX_RUNNING_REQUESTS` to `1`, `4`, `8`, or `16` in both terminals;\nrestart the backend after changing it.\n\n**SGLang Hybrid throughput on the complete seven-benchmark suite.**\n\nD3D-1.7B → Qwen3-8B, concurrency 1, `anchor_num=1`, block size 16,\n`max_new_tokens=512`, greedy decoding, thinking disabled, and natural EOS.\n\n| Dataset | TPS (speedup) |\n|---|---:|\n| GSM8K | 658.10 (4.876×) |\n| MATH-500 | 572.66 (4.243×) |\n| AIME25 | 394.56 (2.924×) |\n| HumanEval | 479.15 (3.550×) |\n| MBPP | 428.39 (3.174×) |\n| LCB-v6 | 267.42 (1.982×) |\n| MT-Bench | 258.54 (1.916×) |\n| **Aggregate** | **501.60 (3.717×)** |\n\nHybrid uses two H800 GPUs; AR uses one. TPS includes\nprefill and generation; startup, tokenization, and warmup are excluded.\nThese are throughput results, not answer-quality scores.\n\n## 🏋️ Training and Layer Pruning\n\nTraining code lives in `train/` and `pruning/`, including\noffline training on target-generated responses, layer selection, physical\npruning, recovery training, and recovery-checkpoint selection.\n\nUse the **same environment** installed above with `requirements.txt` for\ntraining and native inference.\n\n```bash\nexport DRAFT_MODEL=checkpoints/Qwen3-1.7B\nexport TARGET_MODEL=checkpoints/Qwen3-8B\nexport DATA_PATH=data/train.jsonl\nCUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1 NUM_GPUS=2 bash scripts/train.sh \\\n    --attn-implementation sdpa --disable-wandb\n```\n\nDownload the initial checkpoints and prepare the JSONL dataset first. See the\n[training and progressive-pruning guide](docs/training.md) for installation,\ndata schemas, loss settings, and all four pruning stages.\n\n## 🗂️ Repository Guide\n\n```text\nsingle/       Single-request asynchronous draft-and-verify decoding\nserving/      Concurrent decoding, paged KV cache, and AR baselines\nmodels/d3d/   Qwen3-derived D3D draft backbone and compatibility code\nmodels/d3d_training/  Training-specific model port (shared dependencies)\ntrain/        Offline training on target-generated response tokens\npruning/      Layer selection, physical pruning, recovery, checkpoint selection\ncommon/       Shared helpers: devices, checkpoints, datasets, text, metrics\nscripts/      Quick starts, smoke checks, and benchmark entry points\nbenchmarks/   Dataset sources and evaluation protocol\ndocs/         Architecture, model details, and validation notes\ntests/        Model-loading, release, and metric-accounting checks\n```\n\n## Citation & License\n\nD3D-authored code is released under the [MIT License](LICENSE). Included\nthird-party code and Qwen-derived weights retain their own terms; see\n[THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md) and the individual model cards.\n"
 },
 "page:https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.06425": {
  "v": 4,
  "fetched_at": "2026-11-05T04:24:30.818Z",
  "bytes": 5671,
  "text": " \n \n\n [2611.06425] D3D: Decoupled Diffusion Drafting for Asynchronous Speculative Decoding \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n Skip to main content \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Search \n \n \n \n \n \n Submit \n Donate \n \n Log in \n \n \n \n \n Search arXiv \n \n \n \n \n \n Press Enter to search &middot; Advanced search \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n--> \n\n \n \n Computer Science > Artificial Intelligence \n \n\n \n arXiv:2611.06425 (cs)\n \n \n \n \n \n [Submitted on 4 Nov 2026] \n Title: D3D: Decoupled Diffusion Drafting for Asynchronous Speculative Decoding \n Authors: Baoyou Chen , Ruiqiao Mei , Guancong Lin , Tao Song , Weihao Yuan , Qun Liu , Siyu Zhu View a PDF of the paper titled D3D: Decoupled Diffusion Drafting for Asynchronous Speculative Decoding, by Baoyou Chen and 6 other authors \n View PDF \n HTML (experimental) \n\n\n\n \n Abstract: Target-conditioned diffusion drafters predict candidate tokens in parallel, yet each new block must wait for updated target-model hidden states. This forces drafting and verification to run sequentially, limiting speedup even though each block is generated in one pass. We introduce D3D, a standalone diffusion drafter that removes this inter-round dependency. D3D combines blockwise denoising with auxiliary autoregressive supervision to achieve long accepted prefixes without target hidden states. This independence lets D3D draft successor blocks during verification in one packed pass, enabling asynchronous speculative decoding. We progressively prune layers according to their effect on acceptance length to reduce the cost of packed drafting. Removing five of 36 layers retains over 99\\% of mean acceptance length across three benchmarks with Qwen3-8B as the target. Across seven benchmarks, D3D averages 5.00$\\times$ and 5.71$\\times$ decoding speedup with Qwen3-8B and Qwen3-32B targets, compared with 4.03$\\times$ and 3.67$\\times$ for DFlash. On GSM8K with Qwen3-32B, speedup reaches 7.48$\\times$. Code is publicly available at this https URL .\n \n\n \n \n \n Subjects: \n \n Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI) ; Machine Learning (cs.LG) \n \n Cite as: \n arXiv:2611.06425 [cs.AI] \n \n \n \n (or \n arXiv:2611.06425v1 [cs.AI] for this version)\n \n \n \n \n https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2611.06425 \n \n \n Focus to learn more \n \n \n \n arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite (pending registration) \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Submission history From: Baoyou Chen [ view email ] [v1] \n Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:27:58 UTC (1,882 KB) \n \n \n \n \n \n Full-text links: \n Access Paper: \n \n \nView a PDF of the paper titled D3D: Decoupled Diffusion Drafting for Asynchronous Speculative Decoding, by Baoyou Chen and 6 other authors View PDF HTML (experimental) TeX Source\n \n \n \n view license \n \n \n \n Additional Features \n \n Audio Summary \n \n \n \n Current browse context: \n cs.AI \n\n \n \n < prev \n \n | \n next > \n \n \n new \n | \n recent \n | 2026-11 \n \n Change to browse by:\n \n cs \n cs.LG \n \n \n\n \n \n References & Citations \n \n SciX Google Scholar \n Semantic Scholar \n \n \n \n\n \n export BibTeX citation \n Loading... \n \n\n \n \n \n BibTeX formatted citation \n &times; \n \n \n loading... \n \n \n Data provided by: \n \n \n \n \n Bookmark \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Bibliographic Tools \n \n Bibliographic and Citation Tools \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Bibliographic Explorer Toggle \n \n \n \n Bibliographic Explorer ( What is the Explorer? ) \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Connected Papers Toggle \n \n \n \n Connected Papers ( What is Connected Papers? ) \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Litmaps Toggle \n \n \n \n Litmaps ( What is Litmaps? ) \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n scite.ai Toggle \n \n \n \n scite Smart Citations ( What are Smart Citations? ) \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n \n Code, Data, Media \n \n Code, Data and Media Associated with this Article \n \n \n \n \n \n \n alphaXiv Toggle \n \n \n \n alphaXiv ( 