es Integrations Support Customer support Training GitHub Status Company About Partners Changelog GitHub Universe GitHub Universe The event for developers, by developers — talks, workshops, and what’s next for GitHub. Pricing Search / Sign in Sign up Appearance settings \n \n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. \n You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. \n You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. \n\n \n Dismiss alert \n\n\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n {{ message }} \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n rails rails Repository navigation Code Issues 485  ( 485 ) Pull requests 1.3k  ( 1.3k ) Discussions Actions Security and quality 47  ( 47 ) Insights More items \n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n rails \n Security \n Advisories \n GHSA-f3w6-w445-fwh9 \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n \n Possible arbitrary file write and read in Active Storage image analysis\n \n\n \n\n \n\n\n \n \n Critical\n \n \n\n \n flavorjones \n published\n GHSA-f3w6-w445-fwh9 \n Nov 4, 2026 \n\n \n \n \n \n\n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Package \n\n \n \n \n\n \n activestorage \n ( rubygems )\n \n \n \n\n \n Affected versions \n\n >= 8.1, < 8.1.4.1 \n < 8.0.5.2 \n \n\n \n Patched versions \n\n 8.1.4.1 \n 8.0.5.2 \n \n \n\n \n \n\n\n \n \n Description \n \n\n \n \n Impact \n A Rails application that processes attachments with ImageMagick may allow an unauthenticated attacker to write arbitrary files on the server and, when attachments are stored with the Disk service, to read arbitrary files readable by the application process. Those files typically include secret_key_base and credentials for external systems, which may in turn allow escalation to remote code execution or lateral movement to those systems. \n Details \n ImageMagick selects a coder from the content of the file it is given, and some coders act on files named inside the image rather than on the image itself. Active Storage constrained none of ImageMagick's coders, and the ImageMagick analyzer runs when a file is attached, so an attacker who can upload a crafted file may be able to invoke one. Attaching the upload is sufficient; no variant, preview, or analyze call is required. One specific attack chain has been reported to us, but we do not assume it is the only one that exists. \n The fixed versions ship an ImageMagick security policy and prepend its directory to MAGICK_CONFIGURE_PATH through MiniMagick.cli_env , so every ImageMagick process that MiniMagick spawns applies it. The policy denies the MSL scripting coder, the coders that read or delete files other than the image, fetch remote or local references, or display to a screen, every coder backed by Ghostscript together with the gs delegate, and @filename indirection. ImageMagick applies every policy.xml on its search path, so the shipped policy adds to the host's policy rather than replacing it. The policy applies to every ImageMagick command that MiniMagick runs, not only those of Active Storage. See the activestorage CHANGELOG and \"ImageMagick Security Policy\" in the Active Storage guide. \n Affected applications \n An application is affected if it meets all of these requirements: \n \n Uses ImageMagick for Active Storage image processing. This is config.active_storage.variant_processor = :mini_magick , which is the default for applications on load_defaults 6.1 or earlier. \n Runs ImageMagick under a security policy that does not already deny the coders involved. The policies that Debian and Ubuntu package do not. \n Allows file uploads from untrusted users. \n \n Mitigation \n \n Upgrade to a fixed version of activestorage . \n An application whose variant processor is :mini_magick must use mini_magick >= 5.1 , which applying the policy requires. With an older mini_magick, such an application raises an exception during boot. \n An application that renders PostScript or PDF through ImageMagick must re-allow the gs delegate and the coders it uses in the host's policy.xml . \n An application that replaces MiniMagick.cli_env after boot, clears the environment with MiniMagick.cli_prefix , or installs its own MiniMagick::Shell does not receive the shipped policy and must carry its rules in ImageMagick's system policy. GraphicsMagick does not read ImageMagick policies. \n If attachments are stored with the Disk service, change secret_key_base and every secret readable by the application process, including the master key and everything config/credentials.yml.enc holds, storage and database credentials, and third-party tokens. Do not retain an exposed secret as a fallback. \n \n Workarounds \n Copy the rules of the policy that the fixed versions ship, activestorage/lib/active_storage/image_magick/policy.xml , into ImageMagick's system policy, for example /etc/ImageMagick-7/policy.xml . At a minimum, deny the MSL coder, the Ghostscript coders, and the gs delegate: \n < policy domain = \" coder \" rights = \" none \" pattern = \" MSL \" />\n< policy domain = \" delegate \" rights = \" none \" pattern = \" gs \" />\n< policy domain = \" coder \" rights = \" none \" pattern = \" {PS,PS2,PS3,EPS,EPS2,EPS3,EPI,EPSF,EPSI,EPT,EPT2,EPT3,PDF,AI,EPDF,PDFA,POCKETMOD,XPS,PCL} \" /> \n Releases \n The fixed releases are available at the normal locations. \n Patches for those who cannot upgrade at once: \n \n 8.1: 468aa9a \n 8.0: ea8c401 \n \n Versions affected \n \n activestorage < 8.0.5.2 \n activestorage >= 8.1, < 8.1.4.1 \n \n Credit \n This issue was responsibly reported by HackerOne researcher ryotak . \n References \n \n ImageMagick security policy \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n Severity \n \n \n Critical\n \n\n \n \n \n 9.8 \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n CVSS overall score\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n This score calculates overall vulnerability severity from 0 to 10 and is based on the Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS). \n \n \n \n \n / 10 \n \n \n CVSS v3 base metrics \n\n \n Attack vector\n Network \n \n Attack complexity\n Low \n \n Privileges required\n None \n \n User interaction\n None \n \n Scope\n Unchanged \n \n Confidentiality\n High \n \n Integrity\n High \n \n Availability\n High \n \n \n \n Learn more about base metrics \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n CVSS v3 base metrics\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Attack vector: \n More severe the more the remote (logically and physically) an attacker can be in order to exploit the vulnerability. \n \n \n Attack complexity: \n More severe for the least complex attacks. \n \n \n Privileges required: \n More severe if no privileges are required. \n \n \n User interaction: \n More severe when no user interaction is required. \n \n \n Scope: \n More severe when a scope change occurs, e.g. one vulnerable component impacts resources in components beyond its security scope. \n \n \n Confidentiality: \n More severe when loss of data confidentiality is highest, measuring the level of data access available to an unauthorized user. \n \n \n Integrity: \n More severe when loss of data integrity is the highest, measuring the consequence of data modification possible by an unauthorized user. \n \n \n Availability: \n More severe when the loss of impacted component availability is highest. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H \n\n \n\n \n \n CVE ID \n \n No known CVE\n \n \n\n \n Weaknesses \n \n \n Weakness \n CWE-1188 \n \n \n \n Initialization of a Resource with an Insecure Default \n The product initializes or sets a resource with a default that is intended to be changed by the product's installer, administrator, or maintainer, but the default is not secure.\n Learn more on MITRE. \n\n \n \n\n \n\n \n Credits \n\n \n \n \n \n \n Ry0taK \n\n \n Reporter \n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n \n Footer \n\n \n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n &copy; 2026 GitHub, Inc.\n \n \n\n \n Footer navigation \n\n \n\n\n \n Terms \n \n\n \n Privacy \n \n\n\n \n Security \n \n\n \n Status \n \n\n \n Community \n \n\n \n Docs \n \n\n \n Contact \n \n\n \n \n \n \n Manage cookies\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n Do not share my personal information\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n You can’t perform that action at this time.\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n"
 },
