ustomer support Training GitHub Status Company About Partners Changelog GitHub Universe GitHub Universe The event for developers, by developers — talks, workshops, and what’s next for GitHub. Pricing Search / Sign in Sign up Appearance settings \n \n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. \n You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. \n You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. \n\n \n Dismiss alert \n\n\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n {{ message }} \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n rails rails Repository navigation Code Issues 485  ( 485 ) Pull requests 1.3k  ( 1.3k ) Discussions Actions Security and quality 47  ( 47 ) Insights More items \n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n Releases \n v8.1.4.1 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n 8.1.4.1 \n \n Latest \n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n Latest \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n Compare \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n Choose a tag to compare\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Sorry, something went wrong. \n \n \n \n \n \n Filter\n \n \n \n \n \n Loading \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Sorry, something went wrong. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n Uh oh!\n \n There was an error while loading. Please reload this page . \n \n\n \n \n \n \n No results found \n \n \n \n View all tags \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n flavorjones \n\n released this\n\n \n 04 Nov 02:46\n \n \n\n \n \n &middot;\n \n 4786 commits\n \n to main\n since this release\n \n\n\n \n \n \n \n v8.1.4.1\n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n This tag was signed with the committer’s verified signature .\n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n flavorjones \n Mike Dalessio\n \n \n\n \n SSH Key Fingerprint: 0hhJPROywW9jEBOHowjnT+6MkdS+Nd23yTVU4fo+xBs \n Verified\n \n \n Learn about vigilant mode .\n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n 3f290b7 \n \n \n \n\n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n This commit was signed with the committer’s verified signature .\n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n flavorjones \n Mike Dalessio\n \n \n\n \n SSH Key Fingerprint: 0hhJPROywW9jEBOHowjnT+6MkdS+Nd23yTVU4fo+xBs \n Verified\n \n \n Learn about vigilant mode .\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n Active Support \n \n \n ActiveSupport::MessagePack no longer deserializes an unsafe \n ActiveSupport::SafeBuffer as html_safe . \n A SafeBuffer that was no longer html_safe? , for example after an \nin-place gsub! , was deserialized as an html_safe SafeBuffer . It is now \nserialized with an unsafe marker and deserialized as a String . Earlier \nversions of Rails cannot read an unsafe buffer serialized this way. \n [GHSA-2w9f-fxwj-w2qf] \n Jean Boussier \n \n \n ActiveSupport::Inflector#safe_constantize matches the constant name in a \n LoadError message as a literal string instead of building a Regexp \nfrom it. \n The name's segments were interpolated unescaped into the pattern, so input \nthat reaches safe_constantize , such as the channel identifier in an Action \nCable subscribe command, chose the source passed to the regexp compiler. \n [GHSA-8474-xrp6-wh69] \n Jeremy Daer \n \n \n Active Model \n \n No changes. \n \n Active Record \n \n No changes. \n \n Action View \n \n \n Skip attribute names in tag helpers that are blank once converted to a \nstring. \n A Symbol such as :\" \" is not blank, because Symbol#blank? is \n Symbol#empty? , so it reached the escaping step and produced an attribute \nwith no name. The asset helpers symbolize their keys, so an ordinary String \nkey reached the same place. \n [GHSA-68p9-83h6-5wpj] \n Mike Dalessio \n \n \n Fix strip_tags to encode \" and ' in its output. \n strip_tags returns an html_safe string, but was not encoding quotation \nmarks. The method now encodes all five HTML-significant characters ( & , \n < , > , \" , ' ), consistent with the existing html_safe convention. \n Output used outside HTML, such as in a text template or JSON, now contains \n \" and ' where it contained \" and ' . CGI.unescapeHTML \ndecodes them. \n [GHSA-rq8q-p985-fjq7] \n Mike Dalessio \n \n \n Escape the matched phrase before substituting it into highlight 's \n :highlighter . \n A match was copied into each \\1 of the highlighter as it appeared in \nthe sanitized text, which keeps \" and ' as they are, so a match \ncontaining a quote ended a quoted attribute value such as the \ndocumented '<a href=\"search?q=\\1\">\\1</a>' and added attributes of \nits own. Each substituted group now goes through \n ERB::Util.html_escape_once , so quotes in a match render as \" \nand ' . Only the numbered placeholders \\0 to \\9 are expanded, \nand a match never replaces the > that closes a tag. \n [GHSA-v6rj-xm57-3p59] \n Jeremy Daer \n \n \n Require rails-html-sanitizer 1.7.2 or later. \n With the HTML5 sanitizer, Nokogiri before 1.19.5 left < and > \nunescaped in attribute values. highlight and simple_format , which \nedit the sanitized HTML as a string, could then turn markup inside an \nattribute value into live elements. rails-html-sanitizer 1.7.2 requires \nLoofah 2.25.3, which requires Nokogiri 1.19.5. \n [GHSA-2p2f-4rq4-gjwc] \n Mike Dalessio \n \n \n Action Pack \n \n \n Apply config.action_dispatch.cookies_same_site_protection to every session \nstore. \n ActionDispatch::Session::CacheStore , MemCacheStore and third-party \nstores built on AbstractStore or the session mixins sent session cookies \nwith no SameSite attribute. Only CookieStore applied the configured \ndefault. \n [GHSA-gmj8-hvj3-49mw] \n Jean Boussier \n \n \n Prevent ActionController::Live streams from blocking when a full buffer is \nclosed or aborted. \n [GHSA-rwvh-fw6r-pwvp] \n Jeremy Daer \n \n \n Set and extend the Vary header for rendered responses according to the \nrequest headers used in format negotiation. \n Vary: Accept was only added when the request carried a usable Accept \nheader. A response to a request without one, negotiated to HTML or \nJavaScript, could be stored by a shared cache and served to later clients \nthat requested a different representation. \n Responses now vary on Accept and X-Requested-With whenever the format is \nnot given by the URL. XHR requests without Accept also vary on \n Content-Type , which Rails uses as a legacy format fallback. When \n config.action_dispatch.ignore_accept_header is enabled, responses vary \nonly on X-Requested-With . \n These fields are appended to an existing Vary value without duplicating \nfields case-insensitively. Vary: * remains unchanged. \n [GHSA-r9jg-fmfx-2gv6] \n Jeremy Daer \n \n \n Skip writing a CacheStore session that another request deleted while this \none ran. \n A request that loaded a session from ActionDispatch::Session::CacheStore \nwrote it back when it finished, even after a concurrent reset_session or a \nserver-side delete had removed it, so the old session ID worked again. \n [GHSA-2586-8ghr-69fj] \n Mike Dalessio \n \n \n Don't write upgraded cookies to a response that skips the session. \n Reading a signed or encrypted cookie written under a rotated secret, or in \nthe format a :hybrid serializer migrates from, writes it back in the \ncurrent format. That write ignored request.session_options[:skip] , so a \nresponse that skips the session, such as the Active Storage proxy's \npublic, cacheable response, could still carry the session cookie in \n Set-Cookie . Such a response now leaves the cookie unchanged, and a later \nrequest that does not skip the session upgrades it. An application that \nskips the session on every request no longer upgrades its signed or \nencrypted cookies. Cookies the application sets are still written. \n [GHSA-x6mj-8jx9-qhqv] \n Mike Dalessio \n \n \n Detect conflicts between the Forwarded and X-Forwarded-For headers in \n ActionDispatch::RemoteIp . \n When ip_spoofing_check is enabled (the default), requests carrying both \nheaders with conflicting client addresses now raise \n ActionDispatch::RemoteIp::IpSpoofAttackError . \n [GHSA-2gff-2mmg-m73p] \n Gannon McGibbon , Mike Dalessio \n \n \n ActionController::Parameters#each_key returns self when given a block. \n It returned the internal ActiveSupport::HashWithIndifferentAccess , which \ndoes not respond to permitted? , so passing that return value to mass \nassignment skipped the Strong Parameters check. each , each_pair and \n each_value already return self . \n Document that ActionController::Parameters#as_json returns every \nparameter, permitted or not, in a hash that mass assignment does not check. \n [GHSA-wm3x-v3qw-4jh3] \n Mike Dalessio \n \n \n Active Job \n \n No changes. \n \n Action Mailer \n \n No changes. \n \n Action Cable \n \n No changes. \n \n Active Storage \n \n \n Preserve committed proxy responses when a storage error interrupts a \nstreamed download. \n [GHSA-4v2w-w6g6-f8f8] \n Jeremy Daer \n \n \n Derive ActiveStorage::Filename#base and #extension from the sanitized \nfilename. \n This prevents null bytes and invalid byte sequences in stored filename \nmetadata from raising when a blob is opened or represented. Existing blob \nrecords are handled without a data migration. \n [GHSA-p2pm-g2h6-7j5j] \n Jeremy Daer \n \n \n Ship an ImageMagick security policy and apply it to every ImageMagick \nprocess MiniMagick spawns. \n ImageMagick chooses a coder from the content of the file it is given, and \nsome coders act on files named inside the image rather than on the image \nitself. Active Storage constrained none of them, so an uploaded file could \nreach any coder the host's policy allowed, through the ImageMagick analyzer \nat attach time, with no variant or analyze call in the application. \n Active Storage now ships a policy.xml in \n ActiveStorage::ImageMagick::POLICY_DIRECTORY and prepends that directory \nto MAGICK_CONFIGURE_PATH through MiniMagick.cli_env . ImageMagick applies \nevery policy file on its search path, so the shipped policy adds to the \nhost's policy rather than replacing it. A MAGICK_CONFIGURE_PATH set in the \nenvironment or in MiniMagick.cli_env , including by an initializer or \ndotenv, is kept after the shipped directory. \n The shipped policy denies the coders that script ImageMagick ( MSL ), read \nor delete files other than the image ( TEXT , EPHEMERAL ), fetch remote \nreferences ( URL , HTTP , HTTPS , FTP ), display to a screen ( SHOW , \n WIN , PLT ), or hand the file to Ghostscript (the PS , EPS , EPT and \n PDF coders, every alias of them, and the gs delegate), or reach a file \ndirectly ( FILE , MPC , XPS , PCL ), and it refuses @filename \nindirection. The policy applies to every ImageMagick command MiniMagick \nruns, not only Active Storage's. \n These applications must act: \n \n One whose variant processor is :mini_magick has to use mini_magick 5.1 \nor later, which applying the policy requires. With an older mini_magick, \nit raises at boot. \n One that renders PostScript or PDF through ImageMagick has to re-allow \nthe gs delegate and the coders it uses in the host's policy.xml . A \nhost policy that allows a coder overrides the shipped deny. \n One that replaces MiniMagick.cli_env after it boots, clears the \nenvironment with MiniMagick.cli_prefix , or installs its own \n MiniMagick::Shell never receives the shipped policy and has to carry \nits rules in ImageMagick's system policy. So does one that uses \nGraphicsMagick, which does not read ImageMagick policies. \n \n Every other application needs no change. See \"ImageMagick Security Policy\" \nin the Active Storage guide. \n [GHSA-f3w6-w445-fwh9] \n Mike Dalessio \n \n \n Enforce the declared content length on Google Cloud Storage direct uploads. \n The signed URL now requires an x-goog-content-length-range header matching the blob's \n byte_size , so Cloud Storage rejects a body of any other size. \n Browsers send the new header, so a bucket's CORS configuration must list \n x-goog-content-length-range in responseHeader , or direct uploads from the browser fail. \n [GHSA-hfr4-8rjc-97m2] \n Mike Dalessio \n \n \n Sign GCS direct uploads with V2 when cache_control is set. \n V4 signatures did not bind the Content-Type or Content-MD5 headers, so the uploader could \nchoose the stored Content-Type. Direct-upload URLs with cache_control are no longer limited \nto 7 days, and the client sends Cache-Control unsigned. \n [GHSA-3w93-6hmw-whh4] \n Mike Dalessio \n \n \n Stop an uploaded filename choosing the extension of the tempfile Active \nStorage hands to an external tool. \n ActiveStorage::Blob#open named its tempfile after the uploaded filename, \nextension and all. Tools that select a decoder from the extension alone, \nsuch as FFmpeg's AviSynth demuxer on .avs , therefore took their \ninstructions from the uploader. The extension is now kept only when it \ndenotes the blob's recorded media type, and dropped otherwise. \n [GHSA-v924-7rp8-4mxh] \n Mike Dalessio \n \n \n Restrict the formats ffmpeg and ffprobe will open when previewing and \nanalyzing video and audio. \n Active Storage now passes -format_whitelist before the input at every \nffmpeg and ffprobe call site, limiting demuxer selection to common audio and \nvideo container formats. Configure the list with \n config.active_storage.ffmpeg_allowed_formats , or set it to nil to let \nffmpeg choose any demuxer it was built with. \n Files in other formats, such as MXF, DV, AC3, WavPack, AU, W64, and raw \nH.264 or MPEG-1/2 video streams, now fail to preview with \n ActiveStorage::PreviewError , and their analysis stores no media metadata \nand logs a warning. Add their demuxers to the list to keep them. \n config . active_storage . ffmpeg_allowed_formats += %w[ mxf ] \n [GHSA-3f4q-8x5m-76v8] \n Mike Dalessio \n \n \n Action Mailbox \n \n \n Reject Mailgun inbound emails whose timestamp is more than 2 minutes ahead \nof local time. \n [GHSA-5957-c7qm-m469] \n Mike Dalessio \n \n \n Action Text \n \n No changes. \n \n Railties \n \n No changes. \n \n Guides \n \n No changes. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Assets \n 2 \n \n \n \n \n \n Loading \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n Uh oh!\n \n There was an error while loading. Please reload this page . \n \n\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n \n \n --> \n \n \n 👍 \n 2 \n Gabriel1Vitor and EliothMonroy reacted with thumbs up emoji \n 🎉 \n 2 \n larouxn and krpk1900 reacted with hooray emoji \n ❤️ \n 4 \n larouxn, krpk1900, Heliodex, and alexisszabo reacted with heart emoji \n 🚀 \n 3 \n larouxn, krpk1900, and Heliodex reacted with rocket emoji \n \n \n \n All reactions \n \n \n\n \n \n 👍 \n 2 reactions \n \n \n 🎉 \n 2 reactions \n \n \n ❤️ \n 4 reactions \n \n \n 🚀 \n 3 reactions \n \n \n \n \n \n 6 people reacted \n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n \n\n \n\n\n \n \n\n \n\n \n Footer \n\n \n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n &copy; 2026 GitHub, Inc.\n \n \n\n \n Footer navigation \n\n \n\n\n \n Terms \n \n\n \n Privacy \n \n\n\n \n Security \n \n\n \n Status \n \n\n \n Community \n \n\n \n Docs \n \n\n \n Contact \n \n\n \n \n \n \n Manage cookies\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n Do not share my personal information\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n You can’t perform that action at this time.\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n"
