.2\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n v0.25.1\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n v0.25.0\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n v0.24.0\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n v0.23.0\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n Previous Next \n \n \n\n\n \n \n v0.29.0 \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n v0.29.0 \n \n Latest \n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n Latest \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n Compare \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n Choose a tag to compare\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Sorry, something went wrong. \n \n \n \n \n \n Filter\n \n \n \n \n \n Loading \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Sorry, something went wrong. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n Uh oh!\n \n There was an error while loading. Please reload this page . \n \n\n \n \n \n \n No results found \n \n \n \n View all tags \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n github-actions \n\n released this\n\n \n 04 Nov 09:56\n \n \n\n \n\n\n \n \n \n \n v0.29.0\n \n \n \n \n \n 57e2c2c \n \n \n \n\n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n This commit was created on GitHub.com and signed with GitHub’s verified signature .\n \n \n\n\n \n GPG key ID: B5690EEEBB952194 \n \n \n Verified\n \n \n Learn about vigilant mode .\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n Overview \n ggml v0.29.0 adds an OCP FP8 E4M3 tensor type, a new ggml_flash_attn_ext_rows op where each query slice attends to its own list of K/V rows, a batched tensor copy API, and initial support for multi-node tensor parallelism through a new multi-process communicator interface. Core improvements include bounding tensor views by the bytes their strides reach, zero-copy GGUF export of host-buffer tensors, and vm_allocate -based allocations on Apple platforms. Performance work spans all major backends: new SVE kernels in the CPU backend, DPAS flash attention for quantized KV in SYCL, fused MoE MMQ in CUDA, faster MXFP4 mat-vec in Metal, split-K tuning in Vulkan, and a large expansion of quantized GEMM/GEMV coverage in OpenCL. The Hexagon backend gains support for several new ops, including the lightning indexer, top-k mask, conv2d and upscale. \n API changes \n \n Add GGML_TYPE_F8_E4M3 (OCP FP8 E4M3) with float conversion helpers and GGML_FTYPE_MOSTLY_F8_E4M3 ( #27512 ) \n Add ggml_flash_attn_ext_rows() : FA variant where each q slice attends to its own K/V row list via index tensor ( #29510 ) \n Add batched ggml_backend_tensor_copy_n() , ggml_backend_tensor_set_n() and ggml_backend_tensor_get_n() APIs ( #30881 ) \n Add a multi-process communicator interface ( ggml_backend_comm_init_rank_t ) for collectives across separate ranks ( #28967 ) \n \n Core changes \n \n Bound tensor views by the bytes their strides reach and validate strided views against the source extent ( #31584 ) \n GGUF writer: write host-buffer tensor data directly to the output stream without an intermediate copy ( #31144 ) \n Use vm_allocate instead of posix_memalign for large allocations on all Apple platforms ( #31437 ) \n Meta backend: keep tensor splits across permuted views and avoid mirrored splits for ARANGE ( #30499 #30878 ) \n Speed up IQ4 quantization with pre-computed halfway points ( #31201 ) \n \n Backend changes \n CPU \n \n Add SVE 256-bit kernels: MXFP4 GEMV ( #28141 ), Q6_K GEMM ( #27472 ) and q8_0 4x8 GEMV ( #30585 ) \n Gate RVV code on the target vector extension so it is not built for rv64gc without V ( #31607 ) \n Implement ggml_flash_attn_ext_rows ( #29510 ) \n \n CUDA \n \n Add NCCL support for multi-node tensor parallelism via the multi-process communicator, used by the RPC server ( #28967 ) \n Gather batched tensor reads into mapped host memory for the batched copy APIs ( #31391 ) \n Fuse MoE ( MUL_MAT_ID ) gate/up projections with GLU in MMQ ( #31188 ) \n Implement ggml_flash_attn_ext_rows ( #29510 ) \n HIP: enable sparse attention on CDNA ( #31259 ) and add RDNA4_M family for gfx1170/gfx1171 ( #31373 ) \n Fix Q8_1 correction sum in MMQ ( #31247 ) and premature eviction of CUDA graphs ( #30662 ) \n \n SYCL \n \n Add DPAS flash attention kernel for q4_0/q8_0 KV caches on XMX ( #31125 ) \n Vectorize reordered-layout dequantization stores for Q4_0, K-quants, IQ3 and MXFP4 ( #30976 ) \n Add fast ggml_sycl_comm_exchange() for tensor parallelism ( #30956 ) \n Add work-group argmax for short TOP_K rows ( #31110 ) \n Fix f32 -> q2_0/q4_0/q5_0 rounding in CPY ( #31120 ) and FLASH_ATTN_EXT failures ( #30761 ) \n \n Metal \n \n Faster MXFP4 mat-vec; launch unary/binary/GLU kernels with full threadgroups ( #31075 ) \n Implement ggml_flash_attn_ext_rows ( #29510 ) \n Fix cpy kernel for destinations non-contiguous in dim 0 ( #31581 ) \n \n Vulkan \n \n Add tensor-parallel allreduce from shared host buffers ( #25051 ) \n Improve small-n split-K selection on RDNA3/RDNA4 ( #30146 ) and avoid redundant scans when zeroing skipped rows ( #31266 ) \n Skip the maxStorageBufferRange pre-check for non-compute tensors ( #31114 ) \n Fix out-of-bounds NVFP4 UE4M3 scale lookup ( #31079 ) \n \n OpenCL \n \n Add quantized GEMV/GEMM support for Q2_0, IQ1, IQ2, IQ3 and IQ4_XS ( #31340 #31341 #31267 #31338 #31339 ) \n Add tiled Q4_K GEMM and faster Q2_0 GEMV for Adreno ( #30412 #31577 ) \n Add FWHT-accelerated GEMM ( #31434 ) and TOP_K_MASK support ( #31441 ) \n \n Hexagon \n \n Add support for the LIGHTNING_INDEXER ( #31289 ), TOP_K_MASK ( #31552 ), UPSCALE ( #31331 ), CONV_2D ( #30995 ) and DSV4_HC_PRE/POST ( #30953 ) ops \n Faster TOP_K sampler ( #31279 ), block-based HVX IM2COL ( #31050 ), tiled HVX permute ( #31446 ) and better DDR use in transposed CONCAT ( #31277 ) \n Fix DMA transfers with strides larger than 24 bits ( #31442 ) \n \n Other backends \n \n ZDNN: share buffers with host ( #31481 ) and fix a fattn test failure ( #31583 ) \n WebGPU: add ARANGE support ( #31455 ) \n OpenVINO: slice view inputs of SCALE ( #31334 ) \n \n More info \n \n Releases and versioning of ggml-org projects \n \n Changelog since v0.28.0 \n 57e2c2c ggml : bump version to 0.29.0 ( #1680 ) \n 68d509f scripts : add ci-status.sh \n 689e0cb sync : llama.cpp \n f11cb47 ggml : Gate RVV code on the target extension (llama/31607) \n 5c9c721 sync : llama.cpp \n 71b8415 ggml : fix bf16 (llama/31609) \n b8f6efc opencl: improve q2_0 GEMV for Adreno (llama/31577) \n 682dfdd sync : llama.cpp \n 8bdd9c3 ggml: bound views by the bytes their strides reach (llama/31584) \n 02dcc21 ggml : write host-buffer tensor data directly in gguf writer (llama/31144) \n 0c4fecd hexagon: add LIGHTNING_INDEXER support (llama/31289) \n 492ed92 hexagon: add TOP_K_MASK op (llama/31552) \n d88c3d4 hexagon: faster TOP_K for the backend sampler (llama/31279) \n c8e848e hexagon: add DSV4_HC_PRE and DSV4_HC_POST ops (llama/30953) \n 6496f89 ggml-zdnn: fix fattn test failure (llama/31583) \n 781e018 ggml: avoid signed overflow in ggml_roll bounds check (llama/30375) \n 5d3c669 cuda: potential fix for Q8_1 correction sum (llama/31247) \n a044cd3 cuda : gather batched tensor reads into mapped host memory (PR to master) (llama/31391) \n 40c2633 Add nccl support for multi-node tensor parallelism (llama/28967) \n 1030236 meta: support GLM-5.3 next sm tensor (llama/30499) \n 7117df3 metal : fix cpy kernel for dst non-contiguous in dim 0 (llama/31581) \n b4134b7 vulkan: skip maxStorageBufferRange pre-check for non-compute tensors (llama/31114) \n f9be71f delta_net_base: refactor conv state (llama/30878) \n c44f602 vulkan: fix out-of-bounds NVFP4 UE4M3 scale lookup (llama/31079) \n e136ad2 cuda : prevent premature eviction of graphs about to be used (llama/30662) \n 43e15d2 opencl: add initial iq4_xs support (llama/31339) \n cb27aa1 webgpu: add ARANGE support (llama/31455) \n e96dee8 hexagon: tiled hvx permute (llama/31446) \n c33c20d llama : flash_attn_ext_rows - more efficient unified kv for multi-seq (llama/29510) \n 842f76b ggml-zdnn: share buffers with host (llama/31481) \n 643b9af ggml : use vm_allocate instead of posix_memalign on all Apple platforms (llama/31437) \n 2956e59 opencl: add topk_mask (llama/31441) \n aa632fc vulkan: add tensor-parallel allreduce function (llama/25051) \n 122edda vulkan: improve small-n spli... \n Read more \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Assets \n 2 \n \n \n \n \n \n Loading \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n Uh oh!\n \n There was an error while loading. Please reload this page . \n \n\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n \n \n --> \n \n \n \n \n \n All reactions \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n v0.28.0 \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n v0.28.0 \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n Compare \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n Choose a tag to compare\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Sorry, something went wrong. \n \n \n \n \n \n Filter\n \n \n \n \n \n Loading \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Sorry, something went wrong. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n Uh oh!\n \n There was an error while loading. Please reload this page . \n \n\n \n \n \n \n No results found \n \n \n \n View all tags \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n github-actions \n\n released this\n\n \n 28 Oct 10:32\n \n \n\n \n\n\n \n \n \n \n v0.28.0\n \n \n \n \n \n facdc44 \n \n \n \n\n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n This commit was created on GitHub.com and signed with GitHub’s verified signature .\n \n \n\n\n \n GPG key ID: B5690EEEBB952194 \n \n \n Verified\n \n \n Learn about vigilant mode .\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n Overview \n This release adds a fused sparse-attention masking operation ( GGML_OP_TOP_K_MASK ) with CPU, CUDA and Metal implementations, plus accessors to read the precision configured on a compute node. MoE and sparse-attention dispatch got cleaner semantics: an index of -1 in MUL_MAT_ID / ADD_ID now means \"skip this slot\", so backends skip the work and zero the output row instead of relying on out-of-range index patching. The core relaxes SCALE to non-contiguous views and SUM to non-contiguous inputs. Backends gained a lot of throughput: MoE top-k and gate/up+GLU fusions and chunked graph launches on CUDA, graph record/replay and XMX matrix-engine kernels on SYCL, cooperative GEMMs, Q2_K/Q3_K weights and a lightning indexer on OpenCL, subgroup reductions and src1 precision control on Vulkan, and a restructured HTP backend with new repacking and fusion machinery on Hexagon. ZDNN gained flash attention and WebGPU gained Q2_0. \n API changes \n \n New GGML_OP_TOP_K_MASK op and ggml_top_k_mask() - fused top-k sparse attention mask over picks, blocks and extra cells llama/30640 \n New ggml_prec_get_acc() / ggml_prec_get_src() to query the accumulator and per-source precision of a compute node llama/30656 \n ggml_mul_mat_id and ggml_add_id accept -1 as an index: the slot is skipped and the output row is zeroed llama/26631 \n RPC protocol patch version bumped to 8.0.1 for the new op ( GGML_OP_COUNT is now 102) \n \n Core changes \n \n ggml_scale now accepts non-contiguous row views instead of requiring contiguous input llama/31146 \n SUM supports non-contiguous inputs on CPU, CUDA, Vulkan and WebGPU llama/28851 \n MUL_MAT_ID / ADD_ID skip the work for -1 indices in all major backends llama/26631 \n Meta backend: per-expert token scaling for MoE down projections, plus split-state support for the new masking op llama/30861 llama/31081 \n Fix potential counter overflow in ggml_time_ms / ggml_time_us on Windows llama/30969 \n ARGMAX added to the ops that may expand during allocation, avoiding undersized buffers llama/30862 \n RPC: handle oversized RDMA transfers and std::length_error on message receive instead of aborting llama/30399 llama/31204 \n \n Backend changes \n CPU \n \n New CONCAT implementation as a single row kernel covering all types llama/31179 \n KleidiAI: Q8_0 SVE dotprod GEMV and SVE i8mm GEMM kernels, with runtime SVE-i8MM feature detection llama/30808 \n Vectorized v_silu and v_expf , NEON fp32->fp16 conversion, fp32 gelu_quick / geglu_quick without the fp16 table llama/30791 llama/30505 llama/30737 \n Reduce AVX2 tiled accumulators together to cut register pressure in the tiled matmul path llama/30296 \n \n CUDA / HIP \n \n MoE: fused grouped-experts top-k, plus a dedicated fusion path for large expert counts (up to 384) llama/29181 llama/31288 \n Fuse the FFN gate/up matmuls with GLU in MMQ using interleaved gate/up rows; fuse MRoPE with SET_ROWS llama/29948 llama/31025 \n Chunk CUDA graph launches to amortize the launch overhead; clear graphs after a legacy memory pool flush llama/30804 llama/26771 \n Faster MMVQ for low-bit types; MMQ Stream-K capped at available work; DP4A MMQ tile height aligned to the warp size llama/30517 llama/30553 llama/30837 \n SSM_CONV supports kernel size 7; RMS_NORM variants loading float4 and keeping x in registers llama/30873 llama/29720 \n HIP: byte-permute Q1_0 unpacking with a portable fallback; fix bf16 WMMA operand type for gfx11/gfx12 llama/29927 llama/30915 llama/30885 \n Fix shared-memory WAR hazard in vectorized flash attention and a tile-width selection bug in the matmul reduction llama/30573 llama/30836 \n Limit the maximum pinned host buffer size to 4 GB llama/30449 \n \n Metal \n \n Implement TOP_K_MASK llama/31230 \n Optimized ARGMAX and POOL_1D kernels; removed the amax rescaling from the MoE matmul llama/30862 llama/30924 \n Fix 32-bit overflow in large matrix output offsets llama/30072 \n Fix missing MoE kernel variant for 9 experts per token, and a moe_reduce fusion race when dst aliases its inputs llama/30699 llama/30795 \n Fix memory leaks and cleanup logic in the GPU capture path llama/30890 \n \n Vulkan \n \n Support the src1 precision attribute on matmul ops, configurable through the standard precision setters llama/30656 \n RMS_NORM rewritten with subgroup reductions llama/29882 \n Small matmul tiles now use one warp tile per subgroup; larger conv3d tile for coopmat2; clamp coopmat1 int8 prefetch llama/30106 llama/29920 llama/30283 \n Allow dim-3 broadcast in MUL_MAT and fix gpu-visible host memory handling llama/31239 llama/30468 \n \n SYCL \n \n Add graph record and replay to reduce per-op launch overhead llama/28725 \n Restore ESIMD kernels on the FFN path and rework multi-column matmul on Intel XMX matrix engines llama/30239 llama/29864 \n Faster dequantization: fast Q8 path, wide stores for Q4_K/Q5_K, merged fp16/fp32 dequant switches, templated MMVQ/concat launches llama/30775 llama/29696 llama/30740 llama/31013 llama/31008 \n set_tensor_2d for faster tensor-split (KV-cache) loading; bound weight-reorder scratch memory to 32 MiB llama/30358 llama/31062 \n Reordered-quantized weights: fix GET_ROWS , fix prompt-processing regression, support reordered Q8_0 MoE weights llama/30430 llama/30374 llama/29337 \n Flash attention: explicit dependencies instead of host waits in the MKL path, fix crash on mismatched head dimensions llama/30684 llama/30286 llama/30812 \n Fix CONV_2D results for non-contiguous input and an IQ3 crash llama/30363 llama/30604 \n \n OpenCL \n \n Initial Q2_K and Q3_K support across gemv/gemm/mul-mat/mul-id kernels, including MoE variants llama/30999 llama/31172 \n New TOP_K and lightning indexer kernels for sparse attention llama/31026 \n New ops: depthwise CONV_2D , IM2COL_3D , ARGMAX , i32 GET_ROWS and i32/f32 CPY llama/30900 llama/30895 llama/30897 llama/30756 \n More DP4A GEMM coverage: cooperative kernels for Q4_0/Q4_K/Q6_K, vectorized activation loads, extra small-batch variants [llama/30741]( https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull ... \n \n Read more \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Assets \n 2 \n \n \n \n \n \n Loading \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n Uh oh!\n \n There was an error while loading. Please reload this page . \n \n\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n \n \n --> \n \n \n \n \n \n All reactions \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n v0.27.0 \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n v0.27.0 \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n Compare \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n Choose a tag to compare\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Sorry, something went wrong. \n \n \n \n \n \n Filter\n \n \n \n \n \n Loading 