on behaviors. We introduce a plug-in context-management module that selects task-relevant history and maintains concise task-state summaries. On OpenCode, the module improves focus-task completion under same-repository task switching by 5.5 to 15.5 percentage points across the evaluated models. Code is available at github.com/Miraclecsc/Switch-SWE.\",\"upvotes\":6,\"discussionId\":\"6aeaaacf870269964d13a52e\",\"projectPage\":\"https://mqleet.github.io/Switch-Swe/\",\"githubRepo\":\"https://github.com/Miraclecsc/Switch-SWE\",\"githubRepoAddedBy\":\"user\",\"ai_summary\":\"A benchmark for resuming interrupted software tasks reveals performance drops from interleaved work, and a context-management module improves recovery.\",\"ai_keywords\":[\"focus-task resumption\",\"repository-level development\",\"coding agents\",\"cross-task requirement confusion\",\"task-state summaries\",\"context-management module\"],\"ai_summary_model\":\"thinkingmachines/Inkling-Small\",\"githubStars\":26,\"organization\":{\"_id\":\"63e5ef7bf2e9a8f22c515654\",\"name\":\"SJTU\",\"fullname\":\"Shanghai Jiao Tong University\",\"avatar\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/1676013394657-63e5ee22b6a40bf941da0928.png\"}},\"canReadDatabase\":false,\"canManagePapers\":false,\"canSubmit\":false,\"hasHfLevelAccess\":false,\"upvoted\":false,\"upvoters\":[{\"_id\":\"6448b2f53e7b3c11be684348\",\"avatarUrl\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/6448b2f53e7b3c11be684348/QvlUQG3pWf8ZyEVBV6F7w.jpeg\",\"isPro\":true,\"fullname\":\"Qianli Ma\",\"user\":\"Mqleet\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"661d21f306936ccab51d402b\",\"avatarUrl\":\"/avatars/1d82259ecb295eb951bdd42b93e080b6.svg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"Shuochen Chang\",\"user\":\"miraclecsc\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"6a2da6c8ca070ee12c6e396c\",\"avatarUrl\":\"/avatars/d5adda946bf33aa6c75a4da067cc8f69.svg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"Joe Mama\",\"user\":\"JoeMama123123123\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"6571e85f78f54c59a6e4d42e\",\"avatarUrl\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/6571e85f78f54c59a6e4d42e/XASu2zNmM1iNlje2WEzj3.jpeg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"Bo Yang\",\"user\":\"BorisYang326\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"67403d526371a1e86e9d2d91\",\"avatarUrl\":\"/avatars/8ca516ddf3a0c6998afee1a1353e00c4.svg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"Henry\",\"user\":\"vsabcpk\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"6901b520f8f20b9d7015a38d\",\"avatarUrl\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/6901b520f8f20b9d7015a38d/HIlNYBWGOI_XhI9aUJoAl.jpeg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"Shun Zou\",\"user\":\"shunzou05\",\"type\":\"user\"}],\"acceptLanguages\":[\"*\"],\"dailyPaperRank\":0,\"organization\":{\"_id\":\"63e5ef7bf2e9a8f22c515654\",\"name\":\"SJTU\",\"fullname\":\"Shanghai Jiao Tong University\",\"avatar\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/1676013394657-63e5ee22b6a40bf941da0928.png\"},\"markdownContentUrl\":\"https://huggingface.co/buckets/huggingchat/papers-content/resolve/2611/2611.02017.md\",\"query\":{}}\"> Papers arxiv:2611.02017 Copy markdown Switch-SWE: Do Coding Agents Hold Focus When Switching Between Unfinished Tasks? Published on Nov 1 · Submitted by Qianli Ma on Nov 4 · Shanghai Jiao Tong University Upvote 6 Authors: Shuochen Chang , Qianli Ma , Yibo Miao , Qingyang Liu , Bingjie Gao , Haonan Zhao , Siyu Sun , Yulin Sun , Han Zhao , Jiangtong Li Abstract A benchmark for resuming interrupted software tasks reveals performance drops from interleaved work, and a context-management module improves recovery. Generated by thinkingmachines/Inkling-Small Software development sessions often involve several unfinished tasks rather than one issue carried through to completion. As coding agents take on repository-level development , they need to recover an earlier task's requirements and partial progress after intervening work. Existing repository-level benchmarks typically score one issue-to-patch episode and do not directly measure whether an agent can resume a task after advancing other unfinished work in the same repository. We introduce \\ourmethod, a benchmark for focus-task resumption in sessions that interleave unfinished tasks drawn from the same source repository, with a persistent checkout for each task. Each focus task is evaluated in matched uninterrupted and switched sessions with identical focus requirements and executable verifiers. The switched session interleaves ordered stages from other unfinished tasks in the same repository, while only the final focus patch is scored. \\ourmethod~contains 200 focus tasks from 19 Python repositories, reconstructed from issue, pull-request, and review histories and rendered as 400 matched session specifications. Across 7 coding agents , interleaved unfinished work produces an average focus-task resolution gap of 11.5 percentage points, ranging from 6.0 to 15.0 percentage points. Trajectory analysis identifies cross-task requirement confusion and loss of task state as recurrent resumption behaviors. We introduce a plug-in context-management module that selects task-relevant history and maintains concise task-state summaries . On OpenCode, the module improves focus-task completion under same-repository task switching by 5.5 to 15.5 percentage points across the evaluated models. Code is available at github.com/Miraclecsc/Switch-SWE. View arXiv page View PDF Project page GitHub 26 Add to collection Community Mqleet Paper author Paper submitter about 22 hours ago Switch-SWE is a repository-level benchmark for evaluating whether coding agents can resume a focus task after working on other unfinished tasks in the same repository. Each task is evaluated in matched uninterrupted and switched sessions, requiring agents to recover task-specific requirements and partial progress while avoiding cross-task confusion. \n The benchmark provides 200 focus tasks from 19 Python repositories, 400 matched session specifications, and executable verifiers. Across seven coding agents, task switching reduces focus-task resolution by 11.5 percentage points on average. A plug-in context-management module that selects relevant history and maintains task-state summaries improves completion by 5.5–15.5 percentage points on OpenCode. \n 🌐 Paper: https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.02017 🔥 Project Page: https://mqleet.github.io/Switch-Swe/ 🕹️ Code: https://github.com/Miraclecsc/Switch-SWE \n See translation Reply librarian-bot about 3 hours ago This is an automated message from the Librarian Bot . I found the following papers similar to this paper. \n The following papers were recommended by the Semantic Scholar API \n \n WideSWE: Can Coding Agents Coordinate Changes Across Repositories? (2026) \n StateHarness: Maintaining Evolving Project State for Long-Horizon Coding Agents (2026) \n Compact-Bench: Measuring What Context Compaction Costs Long-Horizon Coding Agents (2026) \n PAUSE: Search-Free Steering of Coding Agents Before Their First Source-Code Edit (2026) \n Design and Cross-Domain Evaluation of an Agent Execution Harness (2026) \n Coding-Agent Benchmarks Should Match Their Users'Task Flows (2026) \n FeatureArc: Benchmarking Coding Agents on Evolving Features (2026) \n \n Please give a thumbs up to this comment if you found it helpful! \n If you want recommendations for any Paper on Hugging Face checkout this Space \n You can directly ask Librarian Bot for paper recommendations by tagging it in a comment: @librarian-bot recommend \n See translation Reply Edit Preview Upload images, audio, and videos by dragging in the text input, pasting, or clicking here . Tap or paste here to upload images Comment · Sign up or log in to comment Upvote 6 Get this paper in your agent: hf papers read 2611.02017 Don't have the latest CLI? curl -LsSf https://hf.co/cli/install.sh | bash Models citing this paper 0 No model linking this paper Cite arxiv.org/abs/2611.02017 in a model README.md to link it from this page. Datasets 