  "text": "\n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n Yuxi sandbox isolation failure allows cross-tenant access and internal service compromise · Advisory · xerrors/Yuxi · GitHub \n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n \n\n \n \n\n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n\n \n Skip to content \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n Navigation Menu Sign in Products Platform GitHub Repository hosting, code review, and collaboration Copilot AI coding agent for tasks, projects and automated work Build & Ship Actions CI/CD and automation Code Quality Quality analysis, fixes, and enforcement Codespaces Cloud development environments Secure Code Security Vulnerability detection and remediation Secret Protection Secret scanning and leak prevention All Features Developers Learn Documentation Training Certifications Build Build with Copilot Customize Copilot Integrations Explore Trending repos GitHub Sponsors Developer articles Changelog Changelog Your source for the latest features, improvements, and fixes across GitHub products, all in one place. Businesses By Stage Enterprises Team Startups Nonprofits By Industry Healthcare Financial services Manufacturing Government See all industries Evaluate GitHub Why GitHub Customer Stories Business insights Trust Center Add-ons GitHub Advanced Security Enterprise-grade code security Copilot for business Enterprise-grade AI features Premium Support Enterprise-grade 24/7 support Resources Learn & Connect Documentation Resource center Blog Events & webinars Community Forum Customer Stories Integrations Support Customer support Training GitHub Status Company About Partners Changelog GitHub Universe GitHub Universe The event for developers, by developers — talks, workshops, and what’s next for GitHub. Pricing Search / Sign in Sign up Appearance settings \n \n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. \n You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. \n You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. \n\n \n Dismiss alert \n\n\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n {{ message }} \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n xerrors Yuxi Repository navigation Code Issues 49  ( 49 ) Pull requests Actions Security and quality 2  ( 2 ) Insights More items \n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n Yuxi \n Security \n Advisories \n GHSA-qpm5-6332-9445 \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n \n Yuxi sandbox isolation failure allows cross-tenant access and internal service compromise\n \n\n \n\n \n\n\n \n \n Critical\n \n \n\n \n xerrors \n published\n GHSA-qpm5-6332-9445 \n Aug 24, 2026 \n\n \n \n \n \n\n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Package \n\n \n No package listed \n \n\n \n Affected versions \n\n >= 0.6.0.beta1, < 0.7.1 \n \n\n \n Patched versions \n\n 0.7.1 \n \n \n\n \n \n\n\n \n \n Description \n \n\n \n \n Impact \n Yuxi Docker deployments using the sandbox provisioner are affected by insufficient isolation between execution-capable sandboxes and trusted application services. \n A low-privileged authenticated user who can execute commands in their own sandbox can cross the intended tenant boundary without knowing an administrator password, database password, or MinIO credential. \n Affected deployments may allow a sandbox to: \n \n reach other tenants' sandbox HTTP APIs and access their environment variables, mounted workspace files, uploads, and outputs; \n execute commands in another tenant's active sandbox; \n reach PostgreSQL, Neo4j, MinIO, and other services on the shared application network; \n use shipped default service credentials where those credentials have not been changed; \n enumerate, create, or delete sandboxes through the unauthenticated provisioner management API; and \n obtain command execution in the PostgreSQL container when the exposed database account is a PostgreSQL superuser. \n \n This can result in cross-tenant disclosure of secrets and files, modification of other tenants' data and sandbox state, and denial of \nservice through sandbox deletion. No container escape or kernel vulnerability is required. \n The issue primarily affects Docker Compose deployments that enable execution-capable sandboxes. Deployments in which sandbox functionality is completely disabled and internal services are independently isolated are not affected by the demonstrated attack \npath. \n Patches \n The issue is fixed in Yuxi 0.7.1. \n The patch: \n \n creates a separate Docker network for every dynamically provisioned sandbox; \n permits only the sandbox provisioner to join each sandbox network; \n prevents direct sandbox-to-sandbox and sandbox-to-application-service communication; \n removes direct publication of dynamic sandbox ports; \n requires a deployment-specific SANDBOX_PROVISIONER_TOKEN for all sandbox management and proxy requests; \n returns authenticated proxy URLs instead of direct sandbox container addresses; \n removes production fallback credentials for PostgreSQL, Neo4j, and MinIO; \n reduces unnecessary host-port exposure; and \n documents mandatory credential rotation for existing deployments. \n \n Users should upgrade to Yuxi 0.7.1 or later. \n Upgrading the Compose files does not automatically rotate credentials stored in existing PostgreSQL, Neo4j, or MinIO data volumes. \nExisting deployments must rotate any credentials that were previously set to documented or shipped defaults. \n Workarounds \n If an immediate upgrade is not possible: \n \n Disable sandbox execution, or restrict access to Yuxi to fully trusted administrators. \n Place every sandbox in a network that cannot reach other sandboxes or the application network. \n Block sandbox access to PostgreSQL, Neo4j, MinIO, Redis, and the sandbox provisioner. \n Restrict the provisioner API so that it is reachable only by the Yuxi API and worker services. \n Replace all shipped or historical default credentials with unique, randomly generated credentials. \n Remove PostgreSQL, MinIO, Neo4j, Redis, and provisioner ports from public or untrusted network interfaces. \n Review and rotate secrets stored in user Agent environments if an untrusted user may previously have obtained sandbox execution. \n \n Changing service passwords alone is not a complete workaround because the cross-tenant sandbox API and unauthenticated provisioner paths do not depend on those service credentials. \n References \n \n https://github.com/xerrors/Yuxi \n https://github.com/xerrors/Yuxi/releases/tag/v0.7.1 \n b5b5713 \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n Severity \n \n \n Critical\n \n\n \n \n \n 9.9 \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n CVSS overall score\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n This score calculates overall vulnerability severity from 0 to 10 and is based on the Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS). \n \n \n \n \n / 10 \n \n \n CVSS v3 base metrics \n\n \n Attack vector\n Network \n \n Attack complexity\n Low \n \n Privileges required\n Low \n \n User interaction\n None \n \n Scope\n Changed \n \n Confidentiality\n High \n \n Integrity\n High \n \n Availability\n High \n \n \n \n Learn more about base metrics \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n CVSS v3 base metrics\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Attack vector: \n More severe the more the remote (logically and physically) an attacker can be in order to exploit the vulnerability. \n \n \n Attack complexity: \n More severe for the least complex attacks. \n \n \n Privileges required: \n More severe if no privileges are required. \n \n \n User interaction: \n More severe when no user interaction is required. \n \n \n Scope: \n More severe when a scope change occurs, e.g. one vulnerable component impacts resources in components beyond its security scope. \n \n \n Confidentiality: \n More severe when loss of data confidentiality is highest, measuring the level of data access available to an unauthorized user. \n \n \n Integrity: \n More severe when loss of data integrity is the highest, measuring the consequence of data modification possible by an unauthorized user. \n \n \n Availability: \n More severe when the loss of impacted component availability is highest. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H \n\n \n\n \n \n CVE ID \n \n CVE-2026-97693\n \n \n\n \n Weaknesses \n \n \n Weakness \n CWE-77 \n \n \n \n Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in a Command \n The product constructs all or part of a command using externally-influenced input from an upstream component, but it does not neutralize or incorrectly neutralizes special elements that could modify the intended command when it is sent to a downstream component.\n Learn more on MITRE. \n\n \n \n\n \n \n Weakness \n CWE-284 \n \n \n \n Improper Access Control \n The product does not restrict or incorrectly restricts access to a resource from an unauthorized actor.\n Learn more on MITRE. \n\n \n \n\n \n \n Weakness \n CWE-522 \n \n \n \n Insufficiently Protected Credentials \n The product transmits or stores authentication credentials, but it uses an insecure method that is susceptible to unauthorized interception and/or retrieval.\n Learn more on MITRE. \n\n \n \n\n \n\n \n Credits \n\n \n \n \n \n \n noyp-lasso \n\n \n Reporter \n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n ophir7dror \n\n \n Reporter \n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n michaelasso \n\n \n Reporter \n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n \n Footer \n\n \n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n &copy; 2026 GitHub, Inc.\n \n \n\n \n Footer navigation \n\n \n\n\n \n Terms \n \n\n \n Privacy \n \n\n\n \n Security \n \n\n \n Status \n \n\n \n Community \n \n\n \n Docs \n \n\n \n Contact \n \n\n \n \n \n \n Manage cookies\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n Do not share my personal information\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n You can’t perform that action at this time.\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n"
